
Correct explanation
Method	Meaning
FirstOrDefault()	Returns the first matching record or default/null if none exists.
SingleOrDefault()	Returns exactly one matching record or default/null if none exists. Throws exception if multiple records match.
Find()	Searches by primary key. First checks tracked entities in memory, then queries the database if needed.

Example
// First matching employee
var emp = db.Employees.FirstOrDefault(e => e.DepartmentId == 10);

// Exactly one employee expected
var emp2 = db.Employees.SingleOrDefault(e => e.Id == 101);

// Find employee by primary key
var emp3 = db.Employees.Find(101);


Interview trick: SingleOrDefault() throws an exception if more than one matching record exists.
